_passages_482ad6d6f291"],"text":"A later passage names Job in connection with suffering, patience or endurance, and the Lord’s compassionate outcome. That association is disputed in its precise sense: Job’s endurance may describe persistence through the story or its eventual outcome, but it should not be taken to require silent acceptance of abuse or to forbid escape and protection.","verse_refs":["Job 10:1-22","Job 11:1-20","Job 12:1-25","Job 13:1-28","Job 14:1-22","Job 15:1-35","Job 16:1-22","Job 17:1-16","Job 18:1-21","Job 19:1-29","Job 1:1-22","Job 20:1-29","Job 21:1-34","Job 22:1-30","Job 23:1-17","Job 24:1-25","Job 25:1-6","Job 26:1-14","Job 27:1-23","Job 28:1-28","Job 29:1-25","Job 2:1-13","Job 30:1-31","Job 32:1-22","Job 33:1-33","Job 34:1-37","Job 35:1-16","Job 36:1-33","Job 37:1-24","Job 38:1-41","Job 39:1-30","Job 3:1-26","Job 40:1-24","Job 41:1-34","Job 42:1-17","Job 4:1-21","Job 5:1-27","Job 6:1-30","Job 7:1-21","Job 8:1-22","Job 9:1-35"]}],"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Job’s Closing Case"}],"status":"validated","validation_errors":[],"validation_warnings":[]}
